===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|meteorology}} The layer of the Earth's [[atmosphere]] that is directly above the [[stratosphere]] and directly below the [[thermosphere]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Kshudiram Saha|title=The Earth's Atmosphere: Its Physics and Dynamics|publisher=Springer Science & Business Media|isbn=9783540784272|page=102|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Jlb5PtwpkI8C&pg=PA102&dq=%22ozonosphere%22&hl=&cd=2&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22ozonosphere%22&f=false||text=The '''mesosphere''' may be described as the earth's intermediate or middle atmosphere, which separates the thermosphere above from the ozonosphere (or stratosphere) below, both of which are responsible for absorption of most of the ultraviolet part of the solar radiation and preventing it from reaching the earth's surface.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} The part of the Earth's [[mantle]] below the [[asthenosphere]] and above the [[outer core]].

